<reference id="_headinghp41sspkkb7co" xml:lang="en-us">
   <title>Scenario 2 — Graphical Concept</title>
   <shortdesc>Consider a section titled "Ink Tank Assembly" with an &lt;h2&gt; , a &lt;p&gt; describing the</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>assembly</keyword>
        <keyword>locations</keyword>
        <keyword>image</keyword>
        <keyword>Tank</keyword>
        <keyword>Assembly</keyword>
        <keyword>concept</keyword>
        <indexterm>assembly</indexterm>
        <indexterm>locations</indexterm>
        <indexterm>image</indexterm>
      </keywords>
      <prodinfo>
        <prodname></prodname>
      </prodinfo>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
   <refbody>
      <section>
      <p>Consider a section titled "Ink Tank Assembly" with an <codeph>&lt;h2&gt;</codeph>, a <codeph>&lt;p&gt;</codeph> describing the assembly, and an image of the ink tank area wrapped in a <codeph>&lt;figure&gt;</codeph> element with a <codeph>&lt;figcaption&gt;</codeph> reading "Figure 1: Ink tank and cap locations."</p>
         <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
            <title>Image classifies heading as concept</title>
            <tgroup cols="2">
               <colspec colname="c1"/>
               <colspec colname="c2"/>
               <thead>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <b>HTML Input</b>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <b>DITA Output</b>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </thead>
               <tbody>
                  <row>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;h2 id="ink-tank-assembly">Ink Tank Assembly&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>
  The ink tank assembly holds the ink supply for each color channel.
&lt;/p>
&lt;figure>
  &lt;img src="media/ink_tank_area.png" alt="Ink tank and cap locations"/>
  &lt;figcaption>
    Figure 1: Ink tank and cap locations
  &lt;/figcaption>
&lt;/figure></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                     <entry>
                        <codeblock>
&lt;concept id="ink_tank_assembly">
  &lt;title>Ink Tank Assembly&lt;/title>
  &lt;conbody>
    &lt;p>The ink tank assembly holds the ink supply for each color channel.&lt;/p>
    &lt;fig>
      &lt;title>Ink tank and cap locations&lt;/title>
      &lt;image href="media/ink_tank_area.png">
        &lt;alt>Ink tank and cap locations&lt;/alt>
      &lt;/image>
    &lt;/fig>
  &lt;/conbody>
&lt;/concept></codeblock>
                     </entry>
                  </row>
               </tbody>
            </tgroup>
         </table>
<p><b>Result:</b> An image accompanied by descriptive prose does not change the topic type. Because the heading and surrounding text remain descriptive — explaining what something is, with no imperative verb or sequence of actions — the section classifies as concept. The <codeph>&lt;figure&gt;</codeph>/<codeph>&lt;figcaption&gt;</codeph> pair maps to <codeph>&lt;fig&gt;</codeph> with the caption text as its <codeph>&lt;title&gt;</codeph>, nested inside <codeph>&lt;conbody&gt;</codeph>, and the <codeph>alt</codeph> attribute maps to the <codeph>&lt;alt&gt;</codeph> element inside <codeph>&lt;image&gt;</codeph>.</p>
         </section>
   </refbody>
